# Wiki text layer only — the heavy binary archive (per-ticker filings, decks,
# audio, briefings, equity calls, reports) stays UNtracked. Rollback safety net
# for the _wiki synthesis + derived feature artifacts only.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/INDEX.md
!/_wiki/
!/CLAUDE.md
!/automation/
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
# throwaway previews inside _wiki
_wiki/_preview_*.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# full-corpus search index (binary, rebuilt by _tools/build_search_index.py)
_wiki/_data/search.db
# OpenRouter raw weekly snapshots (~5 MB/week; P: mirror keeps them; history.jsonl is the durable record)
_wiki/_data/openrouter/raw/
# GPU source snapshots and downloaded source assets; compact normalized caches are retained.
_wiki/_data/gpu-pricing/raw/
# artifact fragment (claude.ai republish duplicate of _dashboards/openrouter.html)
_wiki/_data/openrouter/openrouter.artifact.html
_wiki/%TEMP%/
# Excel/Office lock files (created while a workbook is open; never content)
~$*
# Sentiment indicator (build_sentiment.py) — raw inputs and big caches stay untracked.
# All are rebuildable: bodies/raw re-fetch from Outlook (sellside_mail_*.ps1), bbg_long
# re-fetches from the Terminal, the parse cache rebuilds in ~10 min on a version bump.
# The small derived panels (panel_weekly, events, sellside_daily, bbg_history,
# earnings_dates) and _dashboards/sentiment.html ARE tracked.
_wiki/_data/sentiment/sellside_mail_bodies.jsonl
_wiki/_data/sentiment/sellside_mail_bodies.ids
_wiki/_data/sentiment/sellside_mail_raw.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/sellside_mail_delta.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/sellside_parsed_cache.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/bbg_long.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/panel_long.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/picks.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/leadlag.json
_wiki/_data/sentiment/*.docx
_wiki/_tools/_rpt_tmp/
_wiki/_data/sentiment/lab.json

# Project research agent definitions and instructions.
!/.codex/
/.codex/*
!/.codex/agents/
/.codex/agents/*
!/.codex/agents/*.toml
!/.codex/agents/*.md
# Raw Outlook dumps inside dated research folders (~25 MB/run, rebuildable from the
# mailbox, and this repo is PUBLIC). The derived notes/sources .md stay tracked.
_wiki/_data/research/*/emails_archive*.json
_wiki/_data/research/*/emails_live.jsonl
_wiki/_data/research/*/emails_review.txt
# Broker client workbooks pulled for a single study — licensed source material, same
# rule as `relatórios bons\` (archive stays off GitHub; P: mirror keeps them).
_wiki/_data/retrieved/
